  "comments": [
    {
      "paragraph_index": 1,
      "comment": "T. takaii ABI70S6T cells were grown chemolithoautotrophically in MMJS medium."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 2,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 3,
      "comment": "After culturing in MMJS medium (pH 6.0), which is a modified version of MMJ medium (Takai et al., 2002) supplemented with elemental sulfur (3 % w/v) and with a headspace gas of 80 % H2/20 % CO2 (200 kPa) at 70 oC, the presence of short, motile rods was observed in the most diluted series [<4.0x103 cells (g pumice)-1]."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 4,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 5,
      "comment": "MMJ medium consisted of the following components (L−1 MJ synthetic seawater): 1 ml vitamin solution (Balch et al., 1979), 50 mg sodium selenite, 30 mg sodium tungstate, 1 mg resazurin, 20 g NaHCO3 , 0.5 g cysteine hydrochloride and 0.5 g Na2S.9H2O (Sako et al., 1996; Takai et al., 1999)."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 6,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 8,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 10,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 11,
      "comment": "To prepare the standard medium, 50 mg sodium selenite, 30 mg sodium tungstate and 1 mg resazurin were dissolved in 1L MJ synthetic seawater and the pH of the medium was adjusted to around 7.0 with NaOH before autoclaving."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 12,
      "comment": "After autoclaving, a concentrated solution of vitamins (Balch et al., 1979), NaHCO3, thiosulfate, magnetite, cysteine hydrochloride (pH adjusted to 7.0) and Na2S (pH adjusted to 7.0) were added to the medium."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 13,
      "comment": "These solutions were sterilized separately by autoclaving except for the vitamin solution, which was filter-sterilized."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 14,
      "comment": "The pH of tthe medium was adjusted with H2SO4 or NaOH in an anaerobic chamber under 90% N2 and 10% H2 if needed."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 15,
      "comment": "The medium was dispensed at 20% of the total bottle or tube volume and the tubes and bottles were sealed tightly with butyl rubber stoppers under a gas phase of 80% H2 and 20% CO2 at 300 kPa."
    }
  ]
}